WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
- The way the press treated us

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.130
and what was acceptable,

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.210
whether it's, you know,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.040
asking me my measurements

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.540
on nationwide television,

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.500
asking me to stand up,

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.700
Barbara Walters did that,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.590
and compared herself to me.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.700
And just this sort of,

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.900
the approach that they had

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.610
in asking me questions

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.020
as a 12-year-old,

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.060
was really just unconscionable.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.950
And, to see that-

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.900
- It like stirs rage.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.190
- [Brooke] It does.
- Yeah.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.023
- It does.

00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:28.680
I mean, as a mom too,
- Mm-hm.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:29.790
- it just breaks my heart

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:30.750
to see that little girl.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.600
But, you know, I went to regular schools,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.010
I went to college.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.650
I always had this knowledge that,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.940
if I don't have something

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.800
that's gonna keep me grounded,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.090
I'm gonna get eaten up

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.230
by this business.
- Yeah.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.330
- I am going to just get lost in it

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.030
and it's gonna, it's
going to obliterate me.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.500
And then what will I have?

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.320
And I knew I needed something grounding.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.700
I knew I needed a family.
- Maybe that's what saved you

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.747
is stepping outside of that
- Absolutely.

00:00:54.747 --> 00:00:56.850
- and doing something, more normal,

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.200
you know.
- And just seeing another,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.493
world and not,

00:01:01.324 --> 00:01:02.610
and being a kid,

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.740
you know, the having
that sort of experience.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.350
And then I also wanted to win.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.183
- Yeah.
- Do you know what I mean?

00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:10.020
I wanted to prove to other people

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.430
but to myself,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.170
that you can't,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.100
I'm right here

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.450
and I have grown
- Yeah.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.500
- into this person

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.670
and I'm like a Weeble,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.170
you're not gonna knock me over.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.040
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:20.970
- Yeah.
- I'm gonna come right back.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.063
So.
(audience applauds)

